<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Korea and Japan</p><h1 class="st-title">Kenmu Restoration</h1><p class="st-meta">1333 CE – 1336 CE · capital Kyoto</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Emperor Go-Daigo's brief attempt to restore direct imperial rule in Japan after the fall of the Kamakura shogunate.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-daigo">Emperor Go-Daigo</a> plotted against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-clan">Hojo</a> regents for years and was exiled to the Oki islands, but he escaped. When the warlords <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashikaga-takauji">Ashikaga Takauji</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nitta-yoshisada">Nitta Yoshisada</a> turned against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a> and destroyed it in 1333, Go-Daigo returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyoto">Kyoto</a> to rule in person, naming his era Kenmu in 1334.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-daigo">Go-Daigo</a> abolished the office of regent and sought to govern through new offices such as the Records Office and a court for rewards. Yet he favoured courtiers over warriors in distributing confiscated lands, and the new regime proved slow and confused, as satirised in the Nijo-gawara lampoons posted in the capital.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1335 Takauji went east to suppress a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hojo-clan">Hojo</a> revolt and then broke with the emperor. He defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kusunoki-masashige">Kusunoki Masashige</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-minatogawa">Minatogawa</a> in 1336, installed a rival emperor and founded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/ashikaga-shogunate">Ashikaga shogunate</a>, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-go-daigo">Go-Daigo</a> fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoshino-nara">Yoshino</a> to found the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/southern-court">Southern Court</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1333 CE – 1336 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22